{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3372","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3372","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3372\",\"parent_revision\":\"9c7966042dc3205f1d88c2168970574920adfce80398218225a5a217ac56d9b6\",\"root_revision\":\"9c7966042dc3205f1d88c2168970574920adfce80398218225a5a217ac56d9b6\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-01\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nbeads_backend.py has three beads-native \\\"shadow\\\" methods -- list_beads_milestones, create_beads_milestone, assign_beads_item_to_milestone -- built specifically because BeadsBackend.supports_milestones=False (ADR-003: beads milestone IDs are string nanoids, the generic WorkItemBackend Protocol methods are int-keyed and can't represent them). These shadow methods have zero callers anywhere in operations.py or server.py. Beads users currently have no milestone functionality at all through the public API -- not the generic path (correctly refused via require_milestone_support/UnsupportedBackendCapabilityError) and not the beads-native path either (simply unreachable).\\n\\nThis is deliberately out of scope for the \\\"wire up assign_item_to_milestone\\\" follow-up to PR #3364: that follow-up only wires the generic, int-keyed operation (a real consumer already exists -- group-items-to-milestone/SKILL.md Step 5 currently shells out to a GitHub-only script). The beads-native trio has no consumer and no request yet, and would require the first backend-named MCP tool in the entire surface (there is currently no beads-specific tool anywhere in server.py) -- a bigger, separate design decision, not a drive-by fix.\\n\\nNot a duplicate of #2666 (that item is about a different symptom -- backend writes lost on sync, not milestone-specific) or the other suggested matches (#2287 parent item, #3054 general doc-drift audit, #3219 commit-message policy, #912 SAM plan storage migration) -- none of those touch beads milestone entry points.\\n\\nDo, if picked up: design and wire real beads milestone support -- likely operations.py functions dispatching on backend.issue_id_type == \\\"string\\\" (the existing pattern at operations.py's _try_create_backend_issue_ref) to the beads-native shadow methods, plus MCP tool(s) with a naming convention that doesn't clash with the generic backlog_list_milestones/backlog_create_milestone/backlog_assign_item_to_milestone tools. Requires a real use case first -- check whether one has emerged before starting.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Code review on PR #3364 (backlog #2287 slice C) + design review for its follow-up PR\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-01\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"34822a6859a198aeaf1a741d3d2ba595bdd967611dea4d15705deedb555bfffe\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABR0i6zg\"}"}